# Per-issue worktrees created by the backlog loop (`worktreeDir` in
# .claude/backlog.json). They live inside the repository so a run can find
# them without a path outside it, which means the repository has to be told
# not to track its own checkouts: an untracked worktree reads as a dirty tree,
# and a dirty tree is one of the cycle's stop conditions.
.claude/worktrees/

# Dagger's workspace lockfile, which pins the image digests and git refs a run
# resolved. Any Dagger command may write it -- `dagger check` on a suite that
# pulls an image is enough -- so tracking it would make every local run dirty the
# tree, and a dirty tree is one of the backlog loop's stop conditions. Dagger's
# own header in the file says to commit it, so this is a deliberate deferral
# rather than a verdict: whether devex adopts workspace lockfiles is decided in
# the follow-up to #440, not here.
dagger.lock
